 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Honestly, a good fence is the best way. If you can't have that, a strong wire net under any open roof can work. Bears learn quickly though, so it needs to be in place before they come near. As near as possible. Bears learn the shortest routes and easy ones, so going right up to the tent encourages them. Make yourself look big. Talk loudly, throw rocks if you have them. Bears usually leave a well used trail soon after something big and loud comes along, so it works without hurting the bear. You' welcome. Bears are amazing creatures, but they do need space. Do your part to give it to them.",
